The subexponential question needs two distinctions: Dixon and Lenstra–Pomerance have rigorous randomized bounds, while the original Schnorr–Lenstra class-number smoothness method is conditional. Smooth-value density also does not by itself derandomize relation collection: a deterministic search needs a time bound and a guarantee that its relations yield a nontrivial factor. I’m making those requirements explicit in the proposed lemmas.
